# The heavy-fight benchmark, state-aware (tests/fight_bench.py): the river fight
# of fight_river.drive with checks on the game's state (DOTHEROES_DEV_STATE=1,
# port/native/dev_state.cpp). In play in the castle's area (17), the route east
# into the river's area (18) -- confirmed, or the drive stops there -- a mark
# (mark.trigger, with DOTHEROES_DEV_KEYS=1) as the encounter begins, 20 rounds of
# swings (4 s each: a direction tap, two sword presses 0.4 s apart, four times)
# each followed by a check that the hero is still in that area and alive,
# and a mark at the end. tests/fight_bench.py measures from the first physics
# step after the first mark to the second mark, or to a death or a departure,
# and classifies each run by how it ended. Needs a save past the sword (SAVES=).
# DOTHEROES_DEV_CANT_DIE=1 keeps a hit from ending the segment (report such runs
# apart; check results again with normal damage).
log TitleMovie 120
sleep 5
press START
sleep 3
press START
sleep 5
press CROSS
state life>0,area==17 60
sleep 3
hold RIGHT 4
hold DOWN 1.5
hold RIGHT 3
hold RIGHT 4
hold RIGHT 4
hold RIGHT 2.5
hold UP 1.5
hold RIGHT 2
state area==18,life>0 20
touch mark.trigger
hold RIGHT 0.15
repeat 2 CROSS 0.35
hold DOWN 0.15
repeat 2 CROSS 0.35
hold LEFT 0.15
repeat 2 CROSS 0.35
hold UP 0.15
repeat 2 CROSS 0.35
state area==18,life>0 1
hold RIGHT 0.15
repeat 2 CROSS 0.35
hold DOWN 0.15
repeat 2 CROSS 0.35
hold LEFT 0.15
repeat 2 CROSS 0.35
hold UP 0.15
repeat 2 CROSS 0.35
state area==18,life>0 1
hold RIGHT 0.15
repeat 2 CROSS 0.35
hold DOWN 0.15
repeat 2 CROSS 0.35
hold LEFT 0.15
repeat 2 CROSS 0.35
hold UP 0.15
repeat 2 CROSS 0.35
